    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "aedf1c65ad5fbfd3a54a4294f8667f0e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"angular-distribution\">Angular distribution</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In the center-of-mass frame let <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(x=\\cos\\theta||)</marimo-tex> and\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta=\\sqrt{1-4m_e^2/s}||)</marimo-tex>. Then\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t=-s\\beta^2(1-x)/2||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(u=-s\\beta^2(1+x)/2||)</marimo-tex>.\nThe shared flux and phase-space methods give\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(d\\Phi_2/(d\\Omega\\,\\mathrm{flux})=1/(64\\pi^2s)||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For Bhabha scattering, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\theta||)</marimo-tex> labels the outgoing electron.\nFor M\u00f8ller scattering either outgoing electron can carry that label:\nthe displayed <strong>event density includes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/2!||)</marimo-tex> on the full sphere</strong>.\nEquivalently, integrate the labeled density over one hemisphere.\nThis factor belongs to phase-space counting; both interfering exchange\namplitudes remain in the squared matrix element.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "7c079c4953ba31c02c6d667e3c90e467",
      "outputs": [
